"""Exact original T42 obligations; authored analyses remain distinct from observations."""
NOTES={
'T42.01.a':('Four successful publications own11..14; failed15 remains with the accepting caller, which closes it. Closing12 invalidates its live identity before reuse. A generation-bound event cannot identify a recycled12.','Two successful callback pins keep the old slot unavailable after descriptor close. Both completions drain without dispatch; only the final decrement permits a new generation. This is a single event-loop discipline; cross-thread queues need synchronization in addition to identity.',['core:lifecycle']),
'T42.01.b':('The production admission loop makes at most4 attempts: interrupted retries; would-block ends the batch; flags failure closes the privately owned descriptor without publishing. A readable listener is not a promise that accept succeeds.','The reusable initializer acquires into locals and closes at each of5 injected failure sites. The caller descriptor/address remain byte-identical; /proc/self/fd count returns to baseline before process exit. Actual nonblocking accept on an empty listener independently observes EAGAIN.',['core:admission','linux:initializer']),
'T42.01.c':('Linux owns TCP retransmission. The application owns borrowed input spans, parser fields, response storage and send offsets. Local send acceptance permits only the accepted prefix to leave the application buffer; it does not prove peer consumption.','The existing com_net adapter copies the response and retains its flight packet until acknowledgement. The packet input is overwritten after receive; the response remains unchanged and retransmission reproduces the retained packet without advancing snd_nxt. This is packet-model execution, not physical Ethernet or the new T41 successor.',['core:io','custom:retention']),
'T42.02.a':('The exact46-byte header publishes only on its finalLF; all47 split edges are checked. A coalesced second request remains beyond the returned consumed prefix. A completed header may still leave an unfinished body.','The5-byte body00 80 ff 0d 0a is supplied under every two-way split, including every body edge. The parser returns the same five representation bytes only after the final required byte. Header and request completion are separate states.',['parser:headers46','parser:coalesced','parser:binary']),
'T42.02.b':('Origin-form takes its authority from the unique Host. Absolute-form takes the authority from its request target, while still requiring a syntactically valid single Host. This profile matches the configured DNS/IPv4-style string case-insensitively.','The corpus changes configuration to api.example:91 and192.0.2.9:8081, checks origin and absolute successes, and rejects userinfo, IPv6 literal, empty host, missing/nondecimal port and mismatched authority. The supported subset is lexical; it does not perform DNS lookup or claim every RFC URI form.',['parser:origin','parser:absolute','parser:host-reject']),
'T42.02.c':('Whitespace before the colon, a folded field, embeddedNUL and duplicateHost have separate minimized cases. The first malformed header is rejected under every split; no request is published.','High-bit and zero bytes are valid in the length-delimited body but not structural header controls. The body oracle is a byte vector; no Unicode decoder or strlen determines its extent. High-bit field-value obs-text is not confused with forbidden controls.',['parser:space-colon','parser:fold','parser:nul','parser:duplicate-host','parser:binary']),
'T42.03.a':('Accumulate digits against UINT32_MAX before applying the1024 storage cap. 1025 and4294967295 are representable but oversized413;4294967296 and1025x are invalid400. The historical size_t implementation is preserved; the explicit derived branch uses the previously audited hd_length.','On a16-bit-size_t premise, retain the numeral in uint32_t; only after validating <=1024 convert to the storage extent. No admitted value exceeds SIZE_MAX. The supplied model evaluates the four outcomes independently; the same hd_length is also actually compiled byAVR-GCC14.3 and executed on QEMU arduino-uno with compile-time16-bit-size_t/32-bit-uint32_t assertions, four rejects and admitted1024. No fullHTTPserver or physical-board execution is inferred.',['parser:length','models:size_t16','avr:actual-size_t16']),
'T42.03.b':('DuplicateCL, TE+CL, finalgzip and repeatedchunked are400. A valid gzip,chunked chain needs an unsupported decoder and is501. The cap sentinel deliberately preserves TE+CL rejection before413.','Every rejected wire is followed by an apparentGET and checked under all splits; the parser entersFAILED and consumes no later message. The owned socket peer separately sees exactly one final error and EOF. No second application effect is inferred merely from a correct status.',['parser:framing','socket:reject-and-close']),
'T42.03.c':('The5-byte GET body is consumed even though GET is normally bodyless in common usage. The nextGET begins afterabcde. EOF afterabcd produces400, never a successful empty echo. POST without framing has zero body.','A GET/echo405 and POST/unknown404 still consume the selected5-byte body before normal route response, preserving the next request. An Expect error may terminate early only by explicit final-error-and-close policy.',['parser:method','parser:eof','parser:none-post']),
'T42.04.a':('The wire contains chunk sizes, extension text, CRLF and trailers; onlyabcde is representation data. Zero chunk changes toTRAILERS; it does not publish completion before the final empty line.','Alongside every two-way split, each chunk delimiter has a three-receive partition beforeCR, betweenCR/LF, and after the remaining bytes. Returned total consumed counts wire octets; body_length remains5. Segmentation and API call boundaries are not HTTP messages.',['parser:chunk-ledger']),
'T42.04.b':('Syntactically valid trailerHost and Content-Length are discarded and cannot change the selected authority or framing. Unknown quoted extensions are parsed then ignored.','The escaped quotation/backslash extension is constructed to exactly128 bytes and succeeds. Its129-byte sibling is rejected when the complete size line is evaluated, before the first data byte. This implementation buffers the bounded line and does not claim eager rejection at the129th extension byte.',['parser:trailer-isolation','parser:extension']),
'T42.04.c':('Each incomplete chunk prefix receives EOF and fails. The wrong dataCR case is distinct from missing trailer completion. Body1024/1025, trailer1024/1025, trailerfield8/9 and extension128/129 isolate independent capacities.','The corpus mutates only CR/LF framing octets, leaving the intendedabcde data unchanged. Its expected5-byte representation is counted independently. All selected mutations reject, but neither those finite paths nor a coverage percentage prove all grammar or resource properties.',['parser:chunk-framing-mutation','parser:chunk-eof','parser:chunk-body','parser:trailer-bytes','parser:trailer-fields']),
'T42.05.a':('Health has3 representation octets. HEAD emits zero body but preserves the selected Content-Length, including404 length10 and405 length19 with Allow:POST. The retained historical serializer used reason text withoutLF; the successor explicitly chooses lowercase reason+LF.','The changed error representation c3 a9 0a contains3 octets and2Unicode characters. The serializer accepts an explicit byte extent and reports3, including HEAD metadata when selected. Failed output capacity leaves destination and length unchanged in the successor.',['core:response','parser:response']),
'T42.05.b':('An admissible Expect header enqueues100 immediately, before the body. Invalid framing gets a final error instead. In a pipeline the100 stays behind earlier final bytes.','With one output slot, parsing stops while the prior response is pending. After that slot drains, parsing resumes, publishes100 and again stops until100 drains. The client can then send its body. The owned raw peer waits for100, demonstrating progress without pre-sending the body.',['core:fifo1','core:fifo2','socket:ordered-100-binary']),
'T42.05.c':('The fixture uses epoch1672531200. Actual server mode formats time() UTC through hd_date, while unavailable mode passesNULL and omits Date. Request and output deadlines use CLOCK_MONOTONIC independently of Date.','Both the hosted path and an explicitly copied existing customTCP adapter invoke the same successor serializer with unavailable Date. Header termination, body bytes and Content-Length remain independently parsed. A wall-clock rollback is modeled separately; it never enters the monotonic deadline state.',['core:response','socket:date-modes','custom:no-Date','models:wall-clock']),
'T42.06.a':('The scripted send results4,EINTR,2,EAGAIN,3 retain offsets4,4,6,6,9 and exactly nine source bytes. The source must remain immutable until the operation finishes or aborts; storing an offset does not make a reused buffer safe.','Zero write, a positive result larger than remaining storage and EPIPE each abort without advancing an invalid offset or claiming completion. Kernel EAGAIN is separately exercised by the owned unread TCP peer.',['core:io','linux:blocked-output']),
'T42.06.b':('After four bytes of response1 leave, the remainder remains immutable while request2 queues100. Response1 finishes first, followed by100, followed by request2final. Queue entries retain request sequence identity.','If computation2 completes first, a ready-results table still emits sequence1 before2. The explicit finite cost-order model demonstrates the association rule; the synchronous server does not claim an asynchronous compute pool implementation.',['core:prefix-fifo','models:completion-order']),
'T42.06.c':('Request2close prevents coalesced3 from being parsed. Otherwise request4 announces close and5 is never dispatched. After queued output is locally accepted, shutdownWR precedes a bounded receive discard state.','The actual owned TCP receiver never reads; a bounded prefill forces senderEAGAIN. The flow retains offset0 and aborts at its real15000ms output deadline. This is distinct from the separately measured1000ms receive-drain descriptor reclamation. Prefill is test setup, not an HTTP response or peer-consumption claim.',['core:closing','socket:close-second-drops-third','socket:maximum-four','socket:actual-drain-deadline','linux:blocked-output']),
'T42.07.a':('Total elapsed15000 expires even when14900 is recent progress. The comparison is >= and the total start is never renewed by body progress. Monotonic regression is rejected before unsigned subtraction.','NearUINT64_MAX, compare ordering first and subtract only when now>=start/progress. This avoids overflowing start+duration. A clock wrapping into a smaller value is an invalid observation under this explicit monotonic contract, not silently treated as a small elapsed interval.',['core:deadlines']),
'T42.07.b':('Buffered bytes are consumed before recv0 establishes EOF. A complete half-closed body receives its200 echo; an incomplete declared body receives400. The Linux probe reads five queued bytes before observingEOF.','Interrupted/would-block are wait events and cannot substitute forEOF or alter parser extent. The final body byte establishes completion; intervening no-progress events preserve that state until realEOF. The deterministic callback trace is distinguished from actual kernel error observability.',['core:eof-events','linux:buffered-before-EOF','socket:half-close']),
'T42.07.c':('The actual sizeof ledger includes parser line8193 with terminator, body1024,target1025, two1600-byte output arrays, offsets, clocks and padding. Four connection records plus pool/event buffers and transient serializer scratch are accounted separately from kernel socket memory.','The hosted receive buffer is32 bytes instead of the retained2048, and the queue can have one active slot while preserving all wire caps. Parsing pauses when outputs fill and retains unconsumed input. This reduces input storage; the fixed two-element queue allocation intentionally does not claim a physical allocation reduction from a capacity1 setting.',['core:ledger','socket:capacity1-and2','parser:header-bytes','parser:header-fields','parser:target']),
'T42.08.a':('TE+CL with optimisticGET yields one400close response and zero dispatch of the following bytes. The local raw peer and the parser split corpus observe different boundaries of the same contract.','Two original tiny byte interpreters chooseCL4 or terminatingchunk length5 and disagree on one stream boundary. The repaired shared decision rejects before dispatch. This synthetic local model is not a proxy experiment or remote vulnerability claim.',['parser:framing-te-cl','socket:te-cl-reject-and-close','models:framing-disagreement']),
'T42.08.b':('UnsupportedCONNECT orUpgrade yields a final501 and close. Optimistic bytes remain discarded; no tunnel or upgraded protocol is created.','The flawed local model counts a continuation after rejection; the corrected flow treats close as absorbing. Both actual parser inputs are replayed at every split and the owned socket peer sees only the final response. Original requests remain finite local teaching specimens.',['parser:connect-optimistic','parser:upgrade-optimistic','socket:reject-and-close','models:optimistic']),
'T42.08.c':('Independent raw response parsing checks HEAD lengths, binary echo, ordered100, pipelines and half-close. curl independently exercises GET,HEAD,binaryPOST andExpect. Raw exchanges, commands, server flags, binaries and versions are preserved.','After at least7days an unaided learner must predict a new valid partition and malformed boundary, minimize a disagreement and justify any expected change. The supplied unfamiliar-case recipe is ready; author executions today cannot establish that delayed independent performance.',['socket:raw-and-curl','delayed:unobserved'])
}
